43-## 2026-11-02 (scenarios) — Ryan: the scenario cast is modelled on real small-city gas tariffs, under invented names
44-
45-- **Option 2 (Ryan, 2026-11-02).** The worked bills use a small cast in `scenarios/cast.md`: two city-owned systems (about 500 and about 5,000 meters) whose tariff structure (what is charged, how a rate change splits, deposits, late fees) and rounded rates come from real published Texas city gas tariffs, cited in the cast file, under invented names; one regulated utility as the case where Texas state rules bind; one invented non-Texas set of law rows, to show nothing is hard-coded. *Why:* Kyle checks bills that look like what our first customers send, and the rule questions a real tariff raises surface now rather than at onboarding. *Why not invented tariffs:* Kyle would check arithmetic on numbers nobody charges, and an unrealistic tariff hides rule questions. *Why not real names:* a scenario would then make claims about a real city's current policy, which goes stale and can be misread as the platform's view of that city. `application/places-sources/` covers the law but names no city's tariff, so the tariffs come from a web search. *Cost of changing later:* editing the cast file. *Where it lives:* `scenarios/cast.md` (to be written); the existing GBM fixture catalog is superseded.
